  "query_preview": "..\nAs of 1245 AM Sunday...\n\nKEY MESSAGE 1... Overall dry weather through the upcoming week, with \nsome continued signals for increased shower chances next weekend.\n\nThe early season Nor'easter presently offshore of the Mid-Atlantic \nstates will continue to move northwest into New Jersey over the next \n12-36 hours. It will linger into the early part of this upcoming \nweek, which will keep the NW flow going across NC. This will \ncontinue to favor seasonable temperatures the next few days. Highs \ntoday and Monday should be around 80. Lows tonight will be in the \nupper 40s and 50s. It will also keep the cloudiness to a minimum as \nthe mid level moisture will evaporate as it spreads south from VA \ninto NC. \n\nAfter the low pressure exits the NE coast mid-week, upper ridging \nwill build from the Plains east into the SE states. This will keep \ndry subsidence all week with temperatures rising to above normal \nlevels during the daytime Wed-Sat. Highs should reach the mid 80s \nwith even a few spots likely near 90 in the Sandhills.  \n\nFinally, a mid/upper trough is expected to develop over the Plains \nlate this week into the weekend. This will bring a better chance of \nshowers to our region by sometime next weekend as the trough \napproaches and the mean flow becomes S-SW.",
